<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Grupo Marino to export cappuccino coffee.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Grupo Marino to export cappuccino coffee.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grupo Marino, coffee industrialists with 6 percent of the Mexican soluble market, will export a new product this year, a director said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The product will be a cappuccino coffee for vending machines,&quot; Javier Lizarraga Mercado, the vice-chairman of the group's coffee unit Cafe Marino said, adding the company was investing close to $1.5 million in the project.</p>
<p>The cappuccino coffee will be sold by the U.S. company  Chock Full O'Nuts, mainly in the Unites States but also in Ireland and part of Denmark. The two formed an joint venture alliance in 1994.</p>
<p>((--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau (523)817-0397))</p>
